'' Array slices obey RFC-0002's lifetime rules (docs/tiko-slices RFC-0003 §7): TKO1059, a span of
'' a local array returned; TKO1057, a span outliving the array it views; TKO1054, a span shared,
'' an array of spans, a span made with new, and a span of slices; TKO1055, a span field in a type
'' that is not 'as view' (a view type may hold one). A span of an 'x()' parameter's array, and of
'' a span parameter, may be returned, and a call taking 'arr()' returns one that borrows arr.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: --dump-ir tests/diagnostics/src/array-slice-life.tiko
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 1
'' EXPECT-OUT: array-slice-life.tiko(3,14): error TKO1059: cannot return a slice of local 'lv'
'' EXPECT-OUT: array-slice-life.tiko(15,21): error TKO1057: 'keep' outlives 'inner', which this slice borrows from
'' EXPECT-OUT: array-slice-life.tiko(18,34): error TKO1054: a span cannot be shared
'' EXPECT-OUT: array-slice-life.tiko(20,5): error TKO1055: type 'holder' holds slice field 'v' and must be declared 'as view'
'' EXPECT-OUT: array-slice-life.tiko(27,27): error TKO1054: a span cannot be an array element
'' EXPECT-OUT: array-slice-life.tiko(28,36): error TKO1054: a span cannot be allocated with new
'' EXPECT-OUT: array-slice-life.tiko(29,25): error TKO1054: a slice cannot be a span element
'' EXPECT-MAX-DIAG: 7
